## Finding the Second Largest Element in an Array (Java)

### Approach 1: Single Pass (Most Efficient) ✅
```java
public class SecondLargest {
    public static int findSecondLargest(int[] arr) {
        if (arr.length < 2) throw new IllegalArgumentException("Array must have at least 2 elements");

        int first = Integer.MIN_VALUE;
        int second = Integer.MIN_VALUE;

        for (int num : arr) {
            if (num > first) {
                second = first;  // old first becomes second
                first = num;     // update first
            } else if (num > second && num != first) {
                second = num;    // update second
            }
        }

        if (second == Integer.MIN_VALUE) throw new RuntimeException("No second largest element found");
        return second;
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int[] arr = {12, 35, 1, 10, 34, 1};
        System.out.println("Second Largest: " + findSecondLargest(arr)); // 34
    }
}
```
**Time:** O(n) | **Space:** O(1)

